<%#
  Common settings — Updates / What's New page (issue #992 split). Emits items only.
%>
<%- include('global-common-changelog-frequency') %>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">
  After iRaceDeck updates, the What's New page (changelog) can open once in your browser
  to show what changed. "Only after updates with new features" skips small bug-fix
  updates; either way the page always lists everything since your last visit.
</div>
<sdpi-item label="Check for new versions">
  <sdpi-checkbox
    setting="updateCheck"
    label="Tell me when a newer version is available"
    global
    default="true"
  ></sdpi-checkbox>
</sdpi-item>
<div class="ird-supporting-text">
  When this is on, iRaceDeck asks iracedeck.com once an hour — only while this window is
  open — whether a newer version has been released, and lists what is in it below. Turn it
  off and iRaceDeck never contacts the website on its own; the release notes this version
  ships stay exactly as they are.
</div>
